# Committed on purpose, and read by `vite build` because its mode is
# "production". Everything here is compiled into the bundle every visitor
# downloads, so it holds one public fact and nothing else — the API's address.
# There is no secret to leak: the admin session is an httpOnly cookie the API
# sets, and this app never holds a token.
#
# Why it is committed rather than set on the deployment: Vite reads VITE_* at
# BUILD time, so a variable that only exists at runtime is a variable the bundle
# never saw. A build that ran without it throws "VITE_API_BASE_URL is not set"
# in the browser — a blank panel caused by a value nobody thought was missing.
# A default in the repo means the build works anywhere, including a fresh clone.
#
# Still overridable: a real environment variable takes precedence over an .env
# file in Vite, so setting VITE_API_BASE_URL on the deployment wins over this
# without touching the file. Change it here to move the API for everyone.
#
# Must appear verbatim in the API's own CORS_ORIGINS, or every request is
# rejected before it is answered.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.xite.co.in
